# Skills in this directory that an upstream writes, not this repository.
#
# The point of the file is the boundary, not the bookkeeping: anything listed
# here is replaced wholesale by `npx skills update -g`, so a local edit is lost
# on the next update without warning. Extend a vendored skill by writing a
# separate skill beside it that references it. Never edit one in place.
#
# The commit is a record of which upstreams this machine is allowed to
# install, not a lock -- `skills update` resolves the source by name through
# skills.sh and does not write a lockfile for global installs. The trees
# themselves are gitignored: a hundred files of someone else's markdown is
# not this repository.
#
